package in.scrollcount.probe;
final class Privacy {
    static final String DISCLOSURE="ScrollCount uses Android Accessibility to recognise Instagram / Facebook Reels, YouTube Shorts and Snapchat Spotlight and detect when you move between them. With your agreement, it briefly reads their visible UI labels and layout, including while ScrollCount is closed. For supported browsers, it checks supported browsers’ address bars for YouTube Shorts, Instagram Reels and Facebook Reels. Exact video URLs identify browser videos; only on a confirmed YouTube domain may it also read a scoped Shorts player title and layout. URLs and titles are hashed in memory, never saved or uploaded. Temporary content fingerprints are discarded. Foreground/window package metadata tells it when you leave so timing can stop.\n\nOnly platform, sessions, timestamps, active durations, categories and confirmed-item records are saved on this phone. Other apps' UI, typed text and passwords are not inspected. No captions, creators, messages, media or content URLs are saved or uploaded. There is no screen recording, automated tapping or swiping.\n\nThe optional touch-through badge uses this service to show the combined daily Scrolls count above Reels/Shorts. You can turn it off in Settings. If you separately enable Friends sharing, daily counts derived from this detection are encrypted and shared with accepted friends; otherwise counting is offline.\n\nYou can pause counting, disable Accessibility in Android settings or delete local history at any time. Agree below only if you want this Accessibility access.";
    static final String TEXT="Automatic counting works offline. No analytics or advertising SDK. Accessibility inspects only supported apps and modified apps you explicitly select for detection; other apps provide package/window metadata only. For supported browsers, it checks supported browsers’ address bars for YouTube Shorts, Instagram Reels and Facebook Reels. Exact video URLs identify browser videos; only on a confirmed YouTube domain may it also read a scoped Shorts player title and layout. URLs and titles are hashed in memory, never saved or uploaded. Temporary content fingerprints are discarded. Local history contains platform, sessions, timestamps, active durations and view categories, never captions, creators, messages, URLs, media, typed text or passwords. Android backup is disabled.\n\nThe touch-through live badge is on by default for fresh installations after Accessibility setup; you can turn it off in Settings. Optional notifications are off by default. Local diagnostics are enabled by default and can be disabled in Settings. Diagnostic events stay in bounded memory; debug builds can include sanitized layout trees. Release diagnostics can include bounded Snapchat layout metadata (view classes, geometry and fixed control flags), without UI labels or captions. Exports and diagnostic files are saved or shared only on request. A bounded local service-health log saves lifecycle timestamps, exception types and app-code locations without exception messages or viewed content. Android process-exit reasons are read locally on the diagnostics screen. Clear the health log from that screen. Deleting history does not pause counting.\n\nFriends sharing starts after the profile setup agreement. Reliable sharing and hourly sync are on by default; you can pause sharing or turn hourly sync off from the Friends menu. The selected server stores your name, hashed credential, friendships, invitations, public keys and latest encrypted daily totals per recipient for up to 7 days. P-256 ECDH/HKDF and AES-GCM encrypt totals; private keys remain on your phone. Initial public keys are trusted from the server, then pinned. There is no independent key verification or forward secrecy. The operator can inspect metadata; plaintext counts are not uploaded. Cloudflare processes network metadata such as IP addresses for transport and abuse protection.\n\nFriends syncs on opening, every 30 seconds while visible, after new saved counts in small batches, and around each hour in the background. Android may delay jobs or prevent them after force-stop. Friends can fetch the latest saved update while the sender is offline, but it may be stale. Pause stops future uploads; existing snapshots remain readable until expiry, removal or deletion. Removing a friend deletes server snapshots in both directions. Deleting your sharing profile removes its server keys, snapshots, friendships, invitations and temporary legacy signaling. Previously cached copies on friends' phones cannot be remotely erased. Application request logging is disabled in the supplied deployment. Cloudflare may retain its own security/network records under its privacy policy. D1 recovery copies can retain deleted records for up to 30 days (7 days on the Free plan), without use in normal app operation. Profiles, friendship metadata and public keys remain until you delete your profile; invitations expire after 24 hours and legacy connection details after 2 minutes. Reinstall loses credentials and private keys. Local counting history stays separate.";
    static final String COUNTING="Modified apps: select a renamed app in Settings → Modified apps. It must retain accessible player structure. Same-package modifications use the original profile automatically. Instagram Lite is included under Instagram. Friends combines Instagram, Facebook and Snapchat under Reels for compatibility with older clients.\n\nDaily total: every confirmed Reel or Short, including quick skips. Matches the live badge and adds up across sessions.\nWatched / Seen: at least 2 seconds in a confirmed short-video feed.\nQuick skip: a finished exposure under 2 seconds.\nLonger view: at least 10 seconds; included in Seen.\nAverage per item: feed time divided by seen items plus skips, including the current item.\n\nThe first item counts, and returning to an item can count again. These are exposure estimates, not proof of playback completion. Buffering in a confirmed feed may be included. Comments, sharing screens, app switches and locked-screen time are excluded when detected.\n\nToday follows the phone's local calendar date. A midnight-spanning item is assigned to the day it started. Session time is the sum of active exposures.\n\nSmall split-screen and picture-in-picture players are suspended. Identical YouTube labels, missing accessible content and extremely fast transitions may be missed. Social app updates can affect compatibility.\n\nAfter process death only the last saved checkpoint is recovered. Some recent time can still be lost; no downtime is added. Reminders follow detected active session time and may arrive at the next accessibility event.";
}
